# Response headers for Cloudflare (Workers static assets / Pages).
# GitHub Pages ignores this file entirely, so it is safe to commit before the
# migration happens.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is the point of moving hosts. connect-src is an
# allow-list of every origin this page may talk to, so "your schedule never
# leaves your browser" is enforced by the browser rather than promised by us,
# and anyone can verify it by reading this header.
#
# The two analytics endpoints are the ONLY permitted destinations:
#
# - Cloudflare's beacon reports to THIS origin at /cdn-cgi/rum, not to
#   cloudflareinsights.com - Cloudflare proxies it at the edge. Allowing only
#   that exact path, rather than 'self', keeps every other same-origin request
#   blocked: there is no endpoint on this site that accepts data, and the CSP
#   guarantees the browser would refuse to send any. Do not "simplify" this to
#   'self'; that would quietly widen it.
# - Umami's script (loaded from cloud.umami.is) reports to the exact path
#   gateway.umami.is/api/send. It gives unique visitors and visit duration,
#   which Cloudflare's beacon deliberately does not track.
#
# Both are cookieless and report page views, referrer, browser/country and
# timings. Neither ever receives file contents - the .xer is parsed in memory
# and no code path sends it anywhere.
#
# style-src needs 'unsafe-inline' for the style="..." attributes in the markup
# and the inline <style> block in 404.html. script-src allows only 'self' plus
# the two analytics origins - there is no inline script anywhere, and it stays
# that way.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://cloud.umami.is; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src https://schedulevisualiser.com/cdn-cgi/rum https://cloudflareinsights.com https://gateway.umami.is/api/send; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# Vendored libraries are pinned copies that never change in place; everything
# else is left to Cloudflare's defaults so a forgotten ?v= bump can't strand
# anyone on a stale build.
/js/vendor/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Consider adding HSTS once you have confirmed HTTPS works on the custom domain.
# It is deliberately not enabled here because it is sticky - browsers will
# refuse plain HTTP for the whole max-age and you cannot easily undo it.
#   Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
